{
 "id": "loan_write_off",
 "request": "Collections staff submit loan write-offs by webhook with loan_id, amount and reason. Check the loan in core banking: if it isn't there, isn't in status 'defaulted', or the amount is more than its outstanding balance, reply 422 with {status: 'refused', reason} where reason is 'loan not found', 'loan not defaulted' or 'amount exceeds outstanding', and stop. Up to 5,000 needs one approval from the ops manager (OPS_MANAGER_EMAIL). Over 5,000 and up to 50,000 needs two different credit committee members, one after the other (four eyes, both tasks sent to CREDIT_COMMITTEE_EMAIL). Over 50,000 is refused (422, reason 'needs board approval'): the board handles those offline. Every approval is due within 2 days and is rejected automatically if nobody decides; rejecting needs a reason. When approved, write it in ops_db in one transaction: a write_offs row (loan id, amount, the last approver's comment) and an audit_log row (entity 'loan', the loan id, action 'write_off'). Reply 200 {status: 'written_off'}, or 200 {status: 'rejected', reason: <the approver's comment>}.",
 "apis": [],
 "tables": {},
 "expect": {
  "trigger": "Webhook",
  "must_have_types": [
   "Postgres",
   "Approval",
   "Respond"
  ],
  "max_nodes": 24,
  "min_types": {
   "Approval": 3
  }
 },
